nt-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Autonomous YouTube Engine: Creative Intelligence, Story, Script, and Scene Planning Architecture</span></h1><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">1. Executive Summary</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">This research report establishes the creative intelligence architecture for an autonomous video production engine operating under the direction of Hermes. The goal is to discover and integrate existing, maintainable, and Hermes-compatible capabilities capable of transforming raw research evidence into structured, production-ready narrative scripts, shot lists, and scene execution contracts. Adhering strictly to the architectural directive‚ÄîREUSE, INTEGRATE, ADAPT, REPLACE ONLY WITH EVIDENCE, and CUSTOM BUILD LAST‚Äîthis investigation evaluates open-source software (OSS), model execution frameworks, metadata standards, and multi-agent coordination protocols.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The investigation reveals that end-to-end creative planning can be achieved by composing mature open-source tools under Hermes delegation, eliminating the need to custom-build a narrative engine. Intermediate screenplay generation is best handled via the Fountain plain-text standard, parsed into abstract syntax trees (ASTs) using Python libraries such as fountain-tools and screenplain. Scene breakdown and shot-level asset planning are standardized using OpenTimelineIO (OTIO), an open interchange schema maintained by the Academy Software Foundation that represents multi-track timelines, clips, transitions, and production metadata without requiring compute-intensive pixel rendering. Rigid structural constraints across language model outputs are enforced using finite state machine (FSM) token masking frameworks such as Outlines alongside Pydantic schemas. Narrative claim verification and evidence grounding are validated through evaluation harnesses including DeepEval and DSPy assertions. Role-driven multi-agent orchestration is managed via CrewAI Flows.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">By integrating these existing tools, Hermes functions as the master orchestrator and creative director. Custom development is limited to a lightweight adapter skill that maps parsed Fountain screenplay ASTs into OpenTimelineIO production contracts.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">2. Creative Capability Matrix</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The following matrix maps required creative capabilities across the integration waterfall, evaluating existing tools, project resources, and integration paths.</span></p><table style="border-spacing:0;border-collapse:collapse;margin-right:auto"><thead><tr style="height:0pt"><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:46.8pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Creative Capability</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:46.8pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Hermes Native</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;widt