:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">DeepEval / Assertion Rig</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:117pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Mixed (Deterministic Rules + LLM Eval)</span></p></td><td colspan="1" rowspan="1" style="border-right-style:solid;border-bottom-color:#000000;border-top-width:1pt;border-right-width:1pt;border-left-color:#000000;vertical-align:top;border-right-color:#000000;border-left-width:1pt;border-top-style:solid;border-left-style:solid;border-bottom-width:1pt;width:117pt;border-top-color:#000000;border-bottom-style:solid"><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Combines exact reference matching with LLM semantic evaluation.</span></p></td></tr></tbody></table><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">10. Risks, Licensing, and Maintenance Analysis</span></h2><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Licensing Compatibility</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">All primary candidates feature permissive open-source licenses compatible with commercial deployment:</span></p><ul class="lst-kix_list_7-0 start" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span>*</span><span style="font-style:italic">OpenTimelineIO</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">*: Apache License 2.0.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Screenplain &amp; fountain-tools</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: MIT License.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Outlines</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Apache License 2.0.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Pydantic &amp; Instructor</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: MIT License.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">CrewAI</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: MIT License .</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">DeepEval &amp; DSPy</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Apache License 2.0 / MIT License.</span></li></ul><h3 style="padding-top:12pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Maintenance and Stability Analysis</span></h3><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">While screenplain and fountain-py[span_109](start_span)[span_109](end_span) show lower recent commit frequency, they are mature, feature-complete utility parsers with narrow scopes and minimal dependency footprints. Conversely, OpenTimelineIO is actively maintained by the Linux Foundation and visual effects software vendors, minimizing long-term integration risk. Outlines and CrewAI maintain high release velocities, requiring version pinning to prevent breaking API changes.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">11. Targeted Validation Queue</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">To confirm candidate integrations before deployment, the system executes the following prioritized validation tasks:</span></p><ol class="lst-kix_list_8-0 start" start="1" style="padding:0;margin:0"><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Fountain Parsing &amp; Scene Extraction Test</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Verify that fountain-tools parses complex scripts containing inline citations, scene headings, and voiceover directives into clean Python ASTs without parsing errors.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Pydantic &amp; Outlines Zero-Error Generation Test</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Benchmark Outlines grammar-constrained decoding against local models to confirm 100% compliance with the SceneContract JSON schema across 100 consecutive generation passes.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">OpenTimelineIO Serialization Verification</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Confirm that parsed Scene Contracts successfully build valid OpenTimelineIO track structures with accurate clip durations and metadata payloads that pass official OTIO validation.</span></li><li style="padding:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;line-height:1.0;margin-right:0;margin-left:30pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">DeepEval Claim Traceability Audit</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">: Evaluate the DeepEval factual consistency metric on scripts containing embedded research source tags to confirm detection of introduced factual errors with over 90% accuracy .</span></li></ol><h2 style="padding-top:11.2pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">12. System Provenance and Data Verification Framework</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">To ensure factual integrity, the creative intelligence layer implements source provenance tracking throughout story and script generation. Research intelligence passed to Hermes contains unique source keys, verified factual claims, and supporting evidence passages .</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12.8pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">During script drafting, language models must append source comments immediately following any sentence making a factual assertion. Before scene decomposition, the completed Fountain script is passed to the DeepEval verification harness. DeepEval extracts each asserted claim and evaluates it against the source text using semantic overlap and factual consistency metrics. If a script statement fails validation or lacks supporting research evidence, it is flagged, blocked from scene decomposition, and returned to Hermes for revision. This source-to-script provenance chain ensures that downstream visual production components operate exclusively on verified factual data.</span></p><h4 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:12pt;padding-bottom:12.8pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Works cited</span></h4><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">1. Screenplain - write a screenplay in Fountain - LinuxLinks, https://www.linuxlinks.com/screenplain-write-screenplay-fountain/ 2. Screenplain, https://www.screenplain.com/ 3. GitHub - vilcans/screenplain: Write your screenplay in plain text and, https://github.com/vilcans/screenplain 4. wildwinter/screenplay-tools - GitHub, https://github.com/wildwinter/screenplay-tools 5. wildwinter/fountain-py: A python Fountain script parser - GitHub, https://github.com/wildwinter/fountain-py 6. OpenTimelineIO Documentation - Read the Docs, https://readthedocs.org/projects/opentimelineio-deb/downloads/pdf/latest/ 7. OpenTimelineIO/docs/tutorials/otio-timeline-structure.md at main, https://github.com/AcademySoftwareFoundation/OpenTimelineIO/blob/main/docs/tutorials/otio-timeline-structure.md 8. How OpenTimelineIO Enables AI-Native Creative Workflows, https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OsmVeGtz3Ac 9. Outlines: structured JSON/regex/Pydantic LLM generation, https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/skills/optional/mlops/mlops-inference-outlines 10. How to Use Pydantic for LLMs: Schema, Validation &amp; Prompts, https://pydantic.dev/articles/llm-intro 11. Structured Language Model Generation with Outlines - KDnuggets, https://www.kdnuggets.com/structured-language-model-generation-with-outlines 12. RAGAS, TruLens, DeepEval: LLM Evaluation Frameworks (2026), https://atlan.com/know/llm-evaluation-frameworks-compared/ 13. GitHub - confident-ai/deepeval: The LLM Evaluation Framework, https://github.com/confident-ai/deepeval 14. DSPy, https://dspy.ai/ 15. CrewAI Vs AutoGen: A Complete Comparison of Multi-Agent AI, https://medium.com/@kanerika/crewai-vs-autogen-a-complete-comparison-of-multi-agent-ai-frameworks-3d2cec907231 16. 0069-zenml-io-CrewAI-vs-AutoGen-Which-One-Is-the-Best ... - GitHub, https://github.com/Shiyao-Huang/awesome-agent-evolution/blob/main/raw-social/0069-zenml-io-CrewAI-vs-AutoGen-Which-One-Is-the-Best-Framework-to-Build-AI-Agents-and-Applicat.md 17. A collection of examples that show how to use CrewAI ... - GitHub, https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI-examples 18. OpenTimelineIO - PyPI, https://pypi.org/project/OpenTimelineIO/ 19. Fountain Movie Script Parser ‚Äî JavaScript, Python, C#, C++ - Medium, https://wildwinter.medium.com/fountain-movie-script-parser-javascript-python-c-c-ca088d63d298 20. outlines: Generates structured JSON, XML or code from LLMs using, https://skills.rest/skill/outlines-choice5346 21. GitHub - dottxt-ai/outlines: Structured Outputs, https://github.com/dottxt-ai/outlines 22. Getting Structured Output from the LLM using Pydantic | by Ravi Kumar, https://medium.com/@ravikumar46931/getting-structured-output-from-the-llm-using-pydantic-0bab26b33d31 23. JSON Schema | Pydantic Docs, https://pydantic.dev/docs/validation/dev/concepts/json_schema/ 24. GitHub - crewAIInc/crewAI: Framework for orchestrating role-playing, https://github.com/crewaiinc/crewai 25. The open source, multi-agent platform - CrewAI, https://crewai.com/open-source 26. RAGAS | DeepEval - The LLM Evaluation Framework, https://deepeval.com/docs/metrics-ragas 27. DeepEval vs Ragas | DeepEval - The LLM Evaluation Framework, https://deepeval.com/blog/deepeval-vs-ragas 28. Abonia1/CrewAI-Article-Generator - GitHub, https://github.com/Abonia1/CrewAI-Article-Generator 29. Multi-Agent Blog Writing System - Crew AI - GitHub, https://github.com/Abdulbasit110/Blog-writer-multi-agent/ 30. A parser for the Fountain screenplay format - GitHub, https://github.com/Ovid/fountain-parser 31. opentimelineio.schema - Read the Docs, 